==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**5 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[Hackey]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**4 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
**1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage features a deadly synergy between Techn-Old Hyenas and Hackey: anything hit by Techn-Old Hyena will be warped back, leaving any slow units you might've thought of using here (like [[Cyberpunk Cat|Cyberpunk]] or [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Dr.Nova]]) to get obliterated by Hackey. Because of this, focus on using rusher units like Can Can Cat and Fishman Cat rather than your usual backliners. Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat is extremely good here, being able to deal ridiculous amounts of damage to the Prof. Owlbrowleys sitting behind Techn-Old Hyena, Ragin' Gory, and the Techn-Old Hyenas. Idi:NX's Sage Slayer is also very strong here, being able to deliver high amounts of damage against the Techn-Old Hyenas.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - A viable option here, as his [[Massive Damage]] against black helps manage the Ragin' Gories and deal damage to the Prof. Owlbrowleys.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Their high damage helps kill the Techn-Old Hyena as soon as possible so your units don't get warped back and killed by Hackey.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Can be used with Can Can Cat to chip down the Techn-Old Hyena and keep the peons at bay and deal high damage to other peons.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Can also help chip down the Techn-Old Hyena as he deals absurd amounts of damage per hit, as well as high speed to be able to hit at least once before dying.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] - Her [[Sage Slayer]] allows her to deal high amounts of damage to the Techn-Old Hyenas and the Prof. Owlbrowleys.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Gunduros (Uber Rare Cat)|Ballistic Dragon Gunduros]] - Gunduros is great here due to dealing Massive Damage to both Black and Aliens, on top of having a 100% chance to [[Slow]] and [[Knockback]] the enemies. He does even more damage against the Prof. Owlbrowleys and the Techn-Old Hyenas due to his Sage Slayer ability. He also has a [[Conjure]] you can use in case he's in danger of being hit.
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra/Bazifenix]] - Another viable option here as he pretty much annihilates the Techn-Old Hyenas and also deals decent damage even without his Massive Damage ability.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] - A very good attacker for this stage as he deals [[Insane Damage]] to everything in the field and can Conjure if enemies get too close.

==Trivia==
*Marble Swamp's Japanese name, Sokonashi no Ohajiki-numa (底なしのおはじき沼, "Bottomless Ohajiki Swamp"), refers to ''[[wikipedia:Ohajiki|ohajiki]]'', a marbles-like children's game in which each player flicks small coin-shaped pieces also called ''ohajiki'' at their opponent's pieces.

